    "body": "That is not a change we can make at this point. I'm also not sure that symmetry makes a whole lot of sense for this. Either `set()` would have to treat null and the empty string the same, or `get()` would have to return the empty string rather than null, necessitating the need for a `has()` call in certain circumstances. Neither of which would be very consistent with web platform APIs. See also `getAttribute()`, which was at some point defined to not return null, but nobody implemented it that way. And I think that's been for the better.",
